1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:47,505
There is a wide gap
between the train and the platform.

3
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:50,133
Please watch your step.

4
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,802
The doors are opening.

5
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:58,099
Hey, we're here. We have to go.

6
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,017
Get up.

7
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:04,522
Man, I'm tired.

8
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:08,193
We almost missed our stop.

9
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:14,783
I had fun today. See you tomorrow.

10
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,493
Okay.

11
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,426
Go already.

12
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:52,612
You two are amazing.

13
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:55,740
How did you pull off
such great chemistry so quickly?

14
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,659
Nicely done.

15
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:59,577
I knew you two could do it.

16
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,329
With skills like this,

17
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,164
you'll shut everyone up for good.

18
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:06,626
You two are ready
for the progress recital now, right?

19
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:08,086
-Mr. Do.
-Mr. Do.

20
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:11,422
If we have to perform anyway,

21
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:14,008
how about we audition
for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

22
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:15,969
Noblesse Classical Concert?

23
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:18,263
The one sponsored
by the Seodam Foundation?

24
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:19,848
Yes.

25
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:26,062
I don't know. Even established performers
have trouble getting a spot there.

26
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:28,523
Let's do the progress recital first and--

27
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:29,524
No, sir.

28
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:32,694
I'd rather play at the Noblesse Classical
than at the progress recital.

29
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:36,698
I hope you'll respect
my opinion this time.

30
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,244
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

31
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:43,079
Bye. Take care.

32
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:50,587
Hey.

33
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,506
Why did you tell him

34
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:56,259
you wanted to try out for that concert
without talking to me first?

35
00:02:57,135 --> 00:02:58,469
Oh, sorry.

36
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,514
I'm sorry for not asking first,

37
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,017
but will you go with me on this?

38
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:07,187
The Noblesse Classical Concert
was my goal from the very beginning.

39
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,232
What exactly is it?

40
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:13,610
Why does it have to be that concert?

41
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:16,571
Even for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

42
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:20,742
Fine. Let's see you try.

43
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:23,870
But if I still feel the same way then…

44
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:28,249
you'll need to take responsibility
for what you said.

45
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,837
I can't go into detail right now.

46
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:34,881
But Jeong-yo,

47
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,592
it's an important opportunity for me,

48
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:39,761
so I need your help.

49
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,140
You can do that, right?

50
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:52,398
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

51
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,235
EPISODE 3

52
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:05,870
It sounds a little stiff here.

53
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:08,373
Don't worry about the tempo,
and let it flow naturally.

54
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:12,085
But if I let it flow too much,
wouldn't it lose that Bach feel?

55
00:04:12,168 --> 00:04:13,795
Everyone knows how it should sound.

56
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:16,881
Instead of playing the conventional way…

57
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:26,808
Hey, guys!

58
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,270
-Look who's here with snacks!
-Nice!

59
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:36,192
Hey, that's not how you eat this.
This is how you do it.

60
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:38,736
-It's good, right?
-Yeah.

61
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,615
-Hurry up and eat.
-Hold on.

62
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:46,327
Now one for you, Pi-o.

63
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:49,080
All right. One, two, three!

64
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:13,855
Any word?

65
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:23,489
NOBLESSE CLASSICAL CONCERT
AUDITION RESULT: PASSED

66
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:27,785
Yes!

67
00:06:02,403 --> 00:06:04,739
SCHEDULED GUEST SOLOIST KIM NA-RAE

68
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,710
Grandfather.

69
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:20,338
I…

70
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:24,634
passed the audition
for the Noblesse Classical Concert.

71
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:34,977
Grandfather, I said I passed the audition.

72
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:37,480
You'll come and watch, right?

73
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,567
Grandfather, don't you remember?

74
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:44,028
You said you'd watch me perform
if I got to play there--

75
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:45,863
I said leave! Can't you see I'm busy?

76
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,120
I'll decide whether I go or not.

77
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:21,023
This is so tight and uncomfortable.

78
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,943
I don't know
if I can play properly like this.

79
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:28,030
I don't get it.
Why do all classical musicians wear this?

80
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:29,907
Isn't this an outdated formality?

81
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,035
Hey, take a look at this.
It feels so tight.

82
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:34,370
Is my bow tie on right?

83
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,621
Look.

84
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:37,081
Cut it out.

85
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:40,293
What's with the cold shoulder?

86
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:45,590
Are you nervous?

87
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,593
I'm not nervous, so why are you?

88
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:50,344
You've performed over a hundred times.

89
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:55,933
Wow, you two look amazing.

90
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:58,311
All right. Shall we go?

91
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,442
What's his problem?

92
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:07,737
SEODAM ART CENTER

93
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,447
AN EVENING OF YOUNG VIRTUOSOS

94
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:15,870
-Hello.
-Please place it over here.

95
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,915
Let's move this over a bit.

96
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:44,857
There's a medical emergency.

97
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:08,839
KANG PI-O, CHOI JEONG-YO (PIANO DUET)
J.S. BACH, CANTATA BWV 147, NO. 10

98
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:11,342
Choi Jeong-yo.

99
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:15,888
Choi Jeong-yo?

100
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,576
Hyun-soo.

101
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:38,995
Hello, Seon-ju.

102
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,290
You did a great job.

103
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:44,166
You got those kids here in a month.

104
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,880
It'll be a good performance, right?

105
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,385
We need to show them
what they're up against.

106
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:55,553
You're confident, right?

107
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,684
-Oh.
-I'll see you afterward.

108
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,311
-Okay, see you later.
-All right.

109
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:08,399
Hyun-soo.

110
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,281
Hey, you made it.

111
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,284
Pi-o really wanted to perform here.

112
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,370
It's all thanks to you.

113
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:24,957
No, Pi-o made this happen on his own.

114
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,459
I didn't do anything.

115
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:31,839
By the way, it says Pi-o's partner is

116
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:33,299
-Choi--
-Mr. Do?

117
00:10:33,382 --> 00:10:35,217
Sorry, I'll see you later.

118
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,177
Yes?

119
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,263
Please take your seats.

120
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,398
I can't wait!

121
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:50,941
Settle down.

122
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:15,675
Thank you for joining us today
at the Noblesse Classical Concert.

123
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:18,302
For years, the Noblesse Classical Concert

124
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,971
has earned a stellar reputation
as a launching pad

125
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:23,933
-for discovering and showcasing artists
-I'm okay.

126
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:26,435
who have put Korea on the world stage.

127
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:30,731
Let's welcome to the stage
the rising stars of classical music,

128
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:35,027
starting with our first performers
of the evening.

129
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:36,112
Everyone,

130
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:38,823
please welcome them
with a big round of applause.

131
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,651
There's a medical emergency.

132
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,280
Mom!

133
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:22,616
-Mom!
-What's going on? Are you okay?

134
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,619
-Excuse me, wake up!
-Mom! You're okay, right?

135
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:26,704
Mom!

136
00:12:30,833 --> 00:12:31,667
What's happening?

137
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:49,518
He's having trouble breathing.
What's going on?

138
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,024
What's wrong?

139
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:59,236
What's gotten into you?

140
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,197
Get it together!

141
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,492
What are you doing here?

142
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:06,243
The audience is waiting.

143
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:10,456
You two will not perform today.

144
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,584
Go bring the quartet right now.

145
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:14,960
-Yes, sir.
-Hurry.

146
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:16,170
Wait…

147
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:30,643
Mom.

148
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:32,978
Mom.

149
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:34,730
Mom…

150
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,108
Mom…

151
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:46,992
Jeong-yo.

152
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:49,954
Choi Jeong-yo.

153
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,039
Don't think about anything.

154
00:13:53,707 --> 00:13:54,959
Just focus on my voice

155
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:57,920
and my playing.

156
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,799
I can't. I can't do it.

157
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:05,678
Do you trust me or not?

158
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:08,639
Because I trust you.

159
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,600
We practiced this hundreds of times.

160
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:14,520
What's different now? Absolutely nothing.

161
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,897
Ignore everyone else.

162
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,983
Forget where we are.

163
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,485
Just focus on my playing.

164
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,530
Just like you did in the practice room.

165
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:31,472
Play freely…

166
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:34,934
like that day.

167
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:50,968
It's the boy

168
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:53,095
from the Donghan Junior Piano Competition.

169
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,305
Choi Jeong-yo.

170
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,834
I'm totally blown away.

171
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:30,711
I had no idea he was so amazing.

172
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:31,920
How does he play so well?

173
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:34,631
He was blindfolded
but didn't miss a single note.

174
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,216
It was insanely cool, wasn't it?

175
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,342
I told you guys.

176
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:40,220
He's in a totally different league.

177
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:41,889
-You were so right.
-Totally.

178
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:42,973
Let's go, son.

179
00:19:43,849 --> 00:19:45,809
Excuse me, ladies?

180
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:50,606
Hello.

181
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:53,901
So did you enjoy the concert?

182
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:55,110
Yes, well…

183
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:57,779
I suppose we did.

184
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:04,828
Did it help clear up
any misunderstandings you had about me?

185
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,226
Oh, okay.

186
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:30,062
It's great we made it through, right?

187
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:32,189
Dude!

188
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,691
Hey, cut it out. I can't breathe!

189
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:38,070
Choi Jeong-yo! Kang Pi-o!

190
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:42,407
Great job, you two.

191
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,867
I really mean it.

192
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:46,119
Thank you for doing so well.

193
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:48,956
But what happened in the beginning?

194
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:51,625
Jeong-yo was a little nervous,

195
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:54,002
so I suggested the blindfold.

196
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:56,421
Wow, Pi-o. I'm so proud of you.

197
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,340
How'd you come up with that idea?

198
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:00,842
Yes?

199
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:07,391
Hello, sir.

200
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,852
Did you enjoy the performance?

201
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:12,854
There was a bit of trouble at first.

202
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:13,855
You must've been startled.

203
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:15,524
What happened?

204
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:19,945
It looks like Jeong-yo
suddenly got a little nervous.

205
00:21:20,028 --> 00:21:22,281
Luckily, Pi-o handled the situation well,

206
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:24,157
so they pulled through just fine.

207
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:26,285
I see.

208
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:28,161
Today wasn't half bad.

209
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:32,124
Invite me to your next performance.

210
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:36,211
See you later. I loved the performance.

211
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:46,972
What was that kid's name again?

212
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,307
Who do you mean?

213
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,599
The one next to Pi-o.

214
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:52,144
Oh, it's Jeong-yo. Choi Jeong-yo.

215
00:21:52,728 --> 00:21:54,938
I recruited him myself. Good call, right?

216
00:21:55,897 --> 00:21:57,316
I want to see him play again,

217
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:59,776
so bring him
to the orchestra rehearsal room.

218
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,694
-I will.
-Hey.

219
00:22:00,777 --> 00:22:03,572
If you knew someone that talented,
you should've told me first.

220
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:06,450
I didn't know he was that good.

221
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:09,077
-Seriously.
-Goodness.

222
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,789
Hello, ma'am.

223
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:16,001
Hey, aren't we celebrating?

224
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,714
I should get going.

225
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:23,508
Okay, take care.

226
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:24,968
I really enjoyed the performance.

227
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,011
Thank you.

228
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:29,848
Are you calling it a night?

229
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:32,059
After such a good performance?

230
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:35,312
I'll message you.

231
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:37,814
Okay.

232
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,614
I really enjoyed the performance.

233
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:48,742
Goodness, you've got amazing skills.

234
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:50,077
Thank you.

235
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:52,621
Say hi. This is my mom.

236
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,790
Remember how I told you

237
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:57,459
that she's the head
of a classical music agency?

238
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:00,253
Hello.

239
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:04,341
You haven't signed with
an agency yet, right?

240
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:26,113
What's wrong?

241
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:33,286
What aren't you happy about? Just tell me.

242
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:35,205
What was that?

243
00:23:36,206 --> 00:23:37,374
Why didn't you tell me?

244
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:38,917
-About what?
-Choi Jeong-yo!

245
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:42,629
He's the same kid
who crushed you seven years ago!

246
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:44,423
So? What about it?

247
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:48,009
I played better than ever today,

248
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:51,304
and even Grandfather said
he wanted to see my next performance.

249
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:52,848
Your performance?

250
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:56,101
Sure, you played better than usual.

251
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:57,018
But you know what?

252
00:23:57,519 --> 00:24:00,605
Thanks to you,
that kid pulled off a performance

253
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:01,982
that should've been a disaster.

254
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,275
You basically saved

255
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:05,402
your biggest competition.

256
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:07,696
Mom.

257
00:24:08,363 --> 00:24:11,241
Didn't you see
how well I performed on stage?

258
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:15,120
For the first time in my life,
I enjoyed being on stage

259
00:24:15,203 --> 00:24:17,164
and got the best reaction
from the audience.

260
00:24:17,247 --> 00:24:19,291
You think that's because you did well?

261
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:21,251
Choi Jeong-yo was the star today!

262
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:23,920
The audience didn't care about you.

263
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,548
You think I'm overreacting,
but just watch.

264
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:29,801
Social media will be flooded
with Choi Jeong-yo's name tonight.

265
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:33,430
And you'll sit there like a fool
and let him take first place again!

266
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,516
This won't do.

267
00:24:38,226 --> 00:24:40,687
Start preparing for competitions today.

268
00:24:49,196 --> 00:24:51,990
#ONCE IN A GENERATION TALENT
#BLINDFOLDED PIANIST #CHOI JEONG-YO

269
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:03,084
Pi-o.

270
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,837
I knew you could do it.
Today's performance was the best!

271
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:08,048
I only had eyes for you.

272
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:02,936
Are we really not celebrating?

273
00:26:03,770 --> 00:26:04,771
Can't you come out?

274
00:26:10,026 --> 00:26:10,860
CALLING KANG PI-O

275
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:27,794
MS. YOON

276
00:26:27,877 --> 00:26:29,671
Great job today.

277
00:26:29,754 --> 00:26:31,923
I need you to come somewhere
with me tomorrow.

278
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:07,417
CHOI JEONG-YO:
ARE WE REALLY NOT CELEBRATING?

279
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:15,383
How do you usually practice?

280
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:16,926
Do you have a special routine?

281
00:27:17,010 --> 00:27:17,844
What?

282
00:27:17,927 --> 00:27:20,472
Sorry, I just play however I want.

283
00:27:21,389 --> 00:27:23,016
You play however you want?

284
00:27:23,099 --> 00:27:25,268
Wait, so you're actually a natural?

285
00:27:25,352 --> 00:27:28,855
He's got to be a natural
to play with a rhythm like that.

286
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,982
What's your favorite piece to play?

287
00:27:31,691 --> 00:27:33,652
Rachmaninoff? Liszt?

288
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:36,780
I bet you play Barber or Kapustin well
with your sense of rhythm.

289
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:37,697
Am I right?

290
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:40,492
But can't you see him
playing Schubert too?

291
00:27:40,575 --> 00:27:41,660
Yeah, totally.

292
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:44,829
The way he carries out the phrases
sounds so smooth and deliberate.

293
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:47,832
But he doesn't rush the tempo either.

294
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:50,043
He'd be good at playing slow pieces too.

295
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:51,753
You were amazing.

296
00:27:51,836 --> 00:27:55,423
-Can I watch you practice?
-Sorry. Let's talk later.

297
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:57,676
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

298
00:27:58,677 --> 00:28:00,345
-It's your fault.
-What did I do?

299
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:01,346
Hey, Pi-o.

300
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:04,474
-Did you see my message?
-Yeah.

301
00:28:04,557 --> 00:28:07,560
Then why didn't you reply?

302
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:09,813
That's so mean. I waited all night.

303
00:28:12,023 --> 00:28:14,401
Anyway, let's celebrate sometime.

304
00:28:15,068 --> 00:28:17,570
Thanks to you,
we got through the performance.

305
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:20,323
There's no need for that.

306
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:22,992
I didn't do it just for you.

307
00:28:23,993 --> 00:28:24,953
Come on.

308
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:27,997
But I don't feel comfortable
not thanking you.

309
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:33,169
By the way, I've been thinking.

310
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:37,090
Let's keep going and play more duets.

311
00:28:37,757 --> 00:28:41,720
There are some four-hand pieces
I've really been wanting to play.

312
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:44,222
Oh, and I worked on this yesterday…

313
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:45,682
We're done, Jeong-yo.

314
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,601
I'll be too busy
preparing for competitions.

315
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:51,146
If you want to play, find another partner.

316
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:53,523
Hey.

317
00:28:54,899 --> 00:28:56,276
That's a bit harsh.

318
00:28:56,943 --> 00:28:59,738
I want to do it because it's you,
not just anyone.

319
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:01,656
I get what you mean,

320
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:04,242
but I don't have that kind of time.

321
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:06,661
Find another partner.

322
00:29:19,048 --> 00:29:21,342
Hey, Ji-hye. Why are you calling so early?

323
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:22,469
By any chance,

324
00:29:22,552 --> 00:29:25,972
were you thinking about
signing Choi Jeong-yo?

325
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:29,517
Where is this coming from?

326
00:29:29,601 --> 00:29:30,977
If you were, drop the idea.

327
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:33,229
But if you insist on signing him,

328
00:29:34,105 --> 00:29:36,149
Pi-o will no longer be
part of your agency.

329
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:39,986
And I want to know where Hyun-soo lives.

330
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,197
Oh, well--

331
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,199
I can't take notes right now,

332
00:29:44,991 --> 00:29:46,743
so text me his address.

333
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,337
How did you know where I live?

334
00:29:57,420 --> 00:29:58,630
Can I come in?

335
00:30:16,314 --> 00:30:18,399
-I'll get you some coffee.
-Pi-o.

336
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:21,069
Why did you pair him with that kid?

337
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:23,363
What?

338
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:28,493
You did that on purpose
to make that kid stand out.

339
00:30:28,576 --> 00:30:30,787
What on earth are you talking about?

340
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:32,455
You did it because you hate me.

341
00:30:33,039 --> 00:30:34,040
Because

342
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:35,959
I betrayed you.

343
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:39,379
Fine.

344
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:44,592
It's true that I have
hard feelings toward you.

345
00:30:46,052 --> 00:30:47,262
But that doesn't mean

346
00:30:48,012 --> 00:30:49,514
I'd do something like that

347
00:30:50,598 --> 00:30:52,392
because of the past.

348
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:58,273
I felt guilty about asking you
to take Pi-o under your wing.

349
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:01,901
But I still asked.

350
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,404
Because…

351
00:31:05,071 --> 00:31:06,030
Because…

352
00:31:07,156 --> 00:31:08,658
I'm Pi-o's mother.

353
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:11,494
I felt bad about it,

354
00:31:12,203 --> 00:31:13,288
but I had to…

355
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:16,749
save my son.

356
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:33,725
You have no idea.

357
00:31:34,350 --> 00:31:35,351
You don't know…

358
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:39,480
what Pi-o and I have been through.

359
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:43,443
You saw the way my father treated us.

360
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:46,696
I understand

361
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,198
how tough things were for you.

362
00:31:50,199 --> 00:31:51,701
But don't get the wrong idea.

363
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:56,998
I truly thought pairing them up
would bring out the best in each other.

364
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:58,958
And yesterday's performance…

365
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:03,379
clearly brought out Pi-o's true potential.

366
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:05,965
It's your anxiety.

367
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:10,011
It's playing tricks on your imagination.

368
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:11,220
Ji-hye,

369
00:32:11,971 --> 00:32:15,642
Pi-o is a lot more resilient
than you think.

370
00:32:16,476 --> 00:32:17,393
Then,

371
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:20,313
can you help Pi-o…

372
00:32:22,065 --> 00:32:24,692
place in a competition?

373
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:28,571
You know better than anyone

374
00:32:29,072 --> 00:32:30,698
that the only way to survive this industry

375
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:33,409
is to place
in an international competition.

376
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,329
Hyun-soo.

377
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:39,165
Help him place in a competition.

378
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:41,793
Please?

379
00:33:09,654 --> 00:33:10,738
Hello.

380
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:13,908
Hi.

381
00:33:15,618 --> 00:33:18,454
I enjoyed the performance yesterday.

382
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:21,082
Thank you.

383
00:33:21,749 --> 00:33:25,003
But I'm quite worried right now.

384
00:33:26,212 --> 00:33:29,799
Pi-o doesn't have time to waste
playing four hands right now.

385
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:33,094
Are you here to pick up Pi-o?

386
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:37,140
Get in, Jeong-yo.

387
00:33:37,223 --> 00:33:39,017
Oh, okay.

388
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:41,019
Goodbye.

389
00:33:44,647 --> 00:33:46,107
Where are you going?

390
00:33:46,607 --> 00:33:49,277
After watching yesterday's concert,

391
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:50,987
Mr. Kang wanted to see Jeong-yo.

392
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:55,950
See you at home.

393
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,125
Mom.

394
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:06,586
Mom?

395
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:11,257
Have you heard or not?

396
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:12,592
About what?

397
00:34:12,675 --> 00:34:15,219
Didn't your grandfather tell you

398
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,680
he asked to see Choi Jeong-yo?

399
00:34:27,648 --> 00:34:30,068
Now do you understand what I'm saying?

400
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:32,779
I knew something was up last night.

401
00:34:33,696 --> 00:34:36,657
This is why you need to
crush the competition from the start!

402
00:34:37,158 --> 00:34:40,787
I asked Hyun-soo to help you prepare
for an international competition.

403
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:42,121
Just focus on that.

404
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:44,916
Snap out of it and pull yourself together!

405
00:34:47,668 --> 00:34:49,504
PRINCIPAL CONDUCTOR'S OFFICE

406
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:54,801
-Mr. Kang?
-Come in.

407
00:34:55,301 --> 00:34:56,219
Let's go inside.

408
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:57,136
Okay.

409
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:01,265
Hello.

410
00:35:02,975 --> 00:35:03,976
Say hello.

411
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:06,020
This is Maestro Kang Seung-woon.

412
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:07,855
He was Mr. Do's teacher.

413
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:11,400
Hello.

414
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:14,862
As I said before,

415
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:17,615
he'll give you plenty of guidance,
so don't be intimidated.

416
00:35:17,698 --> 00:35:19,617
Don't be intimidated?

417
00:35:20,409 --> 00:35:22,829
I called you here
because I wanted to check something.

418
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:04,453
Stop.

419
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:09,876
You don't follow the sheet music.

420
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:12,128
No, sir.

421
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:16,007
Why play the left hand as a block chord
in measure eight instead of rolling it?

422
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,634
Because that makes it sound more lively.

423
00:36:20,303 --> 00:36:22,471
You know what appassionato means, right?

424
00:36:23,931 --> 00:36:25,433
"Passionately," sir.

425
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:28,144
Then why did you play
measure 33 with rubato?

426
00:36:28,227 --> 00:36:29,478
RUBATO: PLAYING WITH CHANGES TO SPEED

427
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:31,063
Allowing some breathing room

428
00:36:31,898 --> 00:36:34,400
actually makes it feel like
a warm breeze is blowing through.

429
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:38,613
I think Chopin would say it's fine.

430
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,782
Chopin's intentions
are written in the score.

431
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:44,160
Are you ignoring the score?

432
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:47,246
The score is just music written down.

433
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:49,624
I only wanted to hear the music itself.

434
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:54,503
What goes through your mind
when you play the piano?

435
00:37:00,009 --> 00:37:01,093
Nothing.

436
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:04,263
I actually try to clear my mind.

437
00:37:10,811 --> 00:37:12,855
Have you ever practiced a piano concerto?

438
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:15,733
No, sir.

439
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:17,526
All right then.

440
00:37:21,614 --> 00:37:23,282
There's an upcoming symphony festival.

441
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:25,952
Audition for the concerto.

442
00:37:39,507 --> 00:37:40,716
Congratulations, Jeong-yo.

443
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:44,387
It's amazing that he made you
such an offer right away.

444
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:48,599
Trust me, this is truly remarkable.

445
00:37:48,683 --> 00:37:51,143
You have no idea, do you?

446
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:52,520
No.

447
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:57,024
Wow, I never expected you
to make such an impression this quickly.

448
00:37:57,733 --> 00:38:00,778
Pi-o might be disappointed
if you land the concerto,

449
00:38:00,861 --> 00:38:02,446
but that can't be helped.

450
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:11,080
After all, I'm the one who recruited you.

451
00:38:12,915 --> 00:38:14,083
-Right.
-You know what?

452
00:38:15,126 --> 00:38:16,252
Close relationship or not,

453
00:38:16,335 --> 00:38:18,879
I have to keep
my work and personal life separate.

454
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,549
I'm sorry, but…

455
00:38:21,632 --> 00:38:22,508
Yes?

456
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:25,177
What exactly is

457
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:28,097
your relationship to Pi-o?

458
00:38:29,223 --> 00:38:30,057
Goodness.

459
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:35,021
You didn't know?

460
00:38:36,063 --> 00:38:38,482
Pi-o is my grandson.

461
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,109
Legally, that is.

462
00:38:41,402 --> 00:38:43,738
But Mr. Kang is his real grandfather.

463
00:38:46,073 --> 00:38:47,366
Mr. Kang and I are married,

464
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:49,702
and he has a family
from his first marriage.

465
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:52,955
That's how Pi-o became my grandson.

466
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:55,458
The adult world
is a bit complicated, isn't it?

467
00:38:56,959 --> 00:38:59,003
Anyway, all you have to do is work hard.

468
00:38:59,086 --> 00:39:01,505
I'll take care of everything else.

469
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:03,799
Jeong-yo.

470
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:08,679
To tell you the truth,

471
00:39:09,388 --> 00:39:13,351
Mr. Kang has spent years looking for
genuine, raw talent to perform with.

472
00:39:15,561 --> 00:39:16,395
I…

473
00:39:18,147 --> 00:39:20,024
-Ms. Yoon.
-Yes?

474
00:39:22,443 --> 00:39:23,569
I'd rather not…

475
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:27,114
audition for the concerto.

476
00:39:30,117 --> 00:39:30,951
What?

477
00:39:49,428 --> 00:39:53,682
WE NEED TO TALK. LET'S MEET UP.

478
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:01,607
We need to talk.

479
00:40:01,690 --> 00:40:03,150
Let's meet up.

480
00:40:03,234 --> 00:40:04,068
UNREAD

481
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:06,112
Seriously?

482
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,322
CALLING KANG PI-O

483
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:31,387
Kang Pi-o.

484
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:35,808
What are you doing here?

485
00:40:36,392 --> 00:40:38,602
Why won't you answer my calls or texts?

486
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:40,813
Was I supposed to?

487
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:42,356
We need to talk.

488
00:40:43,566 --> 00:40:44,817
I have nothing to say.

489
00:40:49,196 --> 00:40:50,948
Why are you acting like this?

490
00:40:51,031 --> 00:40:52,241
What are you mad about?

491
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:53,909
I told you it's not like that.

492
00:40:55,828 --> 00:40:58,747
Are you keeping your distance from me?

493
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,583
Because I'm your competition or something?

494
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:02,084
Stop talking nonsense.

495
00:41:02,168 --> 00:41:03,961
What the hell is it then?

496
00:41:04,879 --> 00:41:07,882
One minute you're nice, then you're mad.
Make up your mind, damn it.

497
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:10,801
Don't piss me off like that.

498
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:12,887
If you're mad about something,
use your words!

499
00:41:16,348 --> 00:41:20,478
All you have to do is mind your business
and stop being so damn needy!

500
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:25,107
I already told you.

501
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:26,901
I didn't play a duet with you
because I wanted to.

502
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:29,945
I did it to become Mr. Do's student.

503
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:32,072
I accomplished my goal,

504
00:41:32,907 --> 00:41:35,159
so I don't want to
waste my energy on you.

505
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:38,954
That's why I want to call it done,
so why the hell do you keep asking?

506
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:43,876
So that's how you'll talk to me?

507
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,378
All right.

508
00:41:47,338 --> 00:41:48,422
Fine.

509
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:50,341
It's my fault.

510
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,677
I acted like a clueless, needy loser.

511
00:41:54,678 --> 00:41:56,388
Man, I had no idea.

512
00:41:58,098 --> 00:41:59,892
I got all excited,
thinking we were friends.

513
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:18,160
Confucianism views humans
not as beings who follow their desires

514
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:21,956
but as individuals
who must strive for moral perfection.

515
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:25,084
That's why its core concept
is benevolence,

516
00:42:26,001 --> 00:42:28,295
which is the mindset of caring for others.

517
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:29,547
Practicing that mindset daily…

518
00:43:24,476 --> 00:43:25,311
Choi Jeong-yo.

519
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:27,146
Wake up.

520
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:29,773
You plan to sleep through class?

521
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:32,359
-Hey, Jeong-yo.
-Hey, wake up.

522
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:33,944
All right, back to class.

523
00:43:34,028 --> 00:43:34,862
Wake up already.

524
00:43:36,071 --> 00:43:37,239
Where's your textbook?

525
00:43:39,033 --> 00:43:39,992
You don't have it?

526
00:43:40,075 --> 00:43:42,703
You punk.
You're in class without your book?

527
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:45,289
Do you come to school to sleep?

528
00:43:46,206 --> 00:43:48,167
Please leave me alone.

529
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:50,419
What did you say?

530
00:43:51,003 --> 00:43:53,213
I said just leave me alone.

531
00:43:54,256 --> 00:43:55,174
Choi Jeong-yo.

532
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:00,638
Come to the teachers' office.

533
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:02,640
Class is over.

534
00:44:14,777 --> 00:44:15,778
Hey, boys.

535
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:18,656
The seniors need to practice soccer,
so they want us outside next period.

536
00:44:18,739 --> 00:44:19,782
Come out, okay?

537
00:44:27,456 --> 00:44:28,415
Center it!

538
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:29,667
Hey, no hitting!

539
00:44:42,262 --> 00:44:43,430
What's your problem?

540
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,683
-What the hell do you want?
-What's going on?

541
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,519
Hey, over here!

542
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:51,814
-What's happening?
-Hey, wait a minute.

543
00:44:51,897 --> 00:44:54,525
-What's going on?
-Break them up!

544
00:44:54,608 --> 00:44:56,276
Stop them! Hey!

545
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,277
Hey!

546
00:44:57,361 --> 00:44:58,445
Get off me!

547
00:44:58,529 --> 00:44:59,947
You little bastards.

548
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:03,992
You want me to put you guys in line?

549
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:51,415
What happened to your face?
Did you get in a fight?

550
00:45:53,459 --> 00:45:54,710
Who did this to you?

551
00:45:56,336 --> 00:45:57,546
You don't need to know.

552
00:45:57,629 --> 00:46:00,132
Of course I need to know.
Just look at your face.

553
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:01,717
Don't you know looks matter for pianists?

554
00:46:01,800 --> 00:46:03,051
Tell me who did this to you.

555
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:05,053
Tell me right now!

556
00:46:08,390 --> 00:46:09,767
Just stop it!

557
00:46:11,351 --> 00:46:13,562
Do you need to
keep tabs on everything I do?

558
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:16,273
I can still play the piano
with a beat-up face!

559
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:19,985
You're smothering me,
so don't pick me up anymore.

560
00:46:20,652 --> 00:46:24,907
I'm so sick and tired
of you acting like this, Mom!

561
00:46:26,325 --> 00:46:27,284
What's gotten into you?

562
00:46:28,786 --> 00:46:30,204
How dare you take it out on me?

563
00:46:31,288 --> 00:46:33,290
Who do you think I'm doing this for?

564
00:46:35,417 --> 00:46:36,376
You're right.

565
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:38,670
Because you're doing this for me

566
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:40,464
and because I know how you feel inside,

567
00:46:40,547 --> 00:46:43,926
I practiced the piano hard
to make you happy.

568
00:46:44,551 --> 00:46:47,513
I worked my fingers to the bone
to make you smile!

569
00:46:49,348 --> 00:46:50,516
But what's the point?

570
00:46:52,893 --> 00:46:53,727
I'm…

571
00:46:55,062 --> 00:46:56,688
not happy at all.

572
00:46:58,649 --> 00:47:02,236
You'll never be happy
unless I'm the best in the world.

573
00:47:02,986 --> 00:47:04,613
So how could I possibly make you happy?

574
00:47:04,696 --> 00:47:05,906
How?

575
00:47:09,368 --> 00:47:10,828
Stop whining.

576
00:47:12,496 --> 00:47:13,997
The competition is just around the corner.

577
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:16,542
You need to focus.

578
00:47:19,169 --> 00:47:20,170
Mom.

579
00:47:24,007 --> 00:47:25,717
I'm falling apart right now…

580
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:29,721
and all you care about
is some competition?

581
00:47:42,234 --> 00:47:43,193
Pi-o.

582
00:47:47,322 --> 00:47:48,365
Kang Pi-o!

583
00:48:00,210 --> 00:48:01,461
How about this piece?

584
00:48:02,170 --> 00:48:05,674
Let's say you enter
the upcoming Harmonie Competition.

585
00:48:05,757 --> 00:48:08,010
Besides the required piece,
the piano concerto…

586
00:48:09,177 --> 00:48:10,012
Pi-o?

587
00:48:11,096 --> 00:48:11,930
Hey, Pi-o.

588
00:48:15,309 --> 00:48:16,143
Yes?

589
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:18,270
Why are you so out of it these days?

590
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:22,691
You think you can prepare
for the competition like this?

591
00:48:25,694 --> 00:48:26,945
I'm sorry.

592
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:49,217
Jeong-yo!

593
00:48:50,761 --> 00:48:53,764
Man, it's been a while.

594
00:48:54,514 --> 00:48:56,642
Come over here for a second.

595
00:48:57,267 --> 00:48:58,352
Your dad ran off, didn't he?

596
00:49:06,193 --> 00:49:07,361
I thought we were close.

597
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:10,530
Why is it so hard to track you down?

598
00:49:13,241 --> 00:49:16,286
I took him in, fed him,
and cut him slack out of pity.

599
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:20,082
And this is how he repays me?

600
00:49:20,916 --> 00:49:22,250
Where's your dad?

601
00:49:22,334 --> 00:49:24,127
I really don't know.

602
00:49:27,422 --> 00:49:28,382
Stand up straight.

603
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:34,554
Life is pretty great for you
these days, isn't it?

604
00:49:35,555 --> 00:49:36,473
Grab him.

605
00:49:36,556 --> 00:49:37,724
What?

606
00:49:38,392 --> 00:49:39,226
I said grab him.

607
00:49:40,811 --> 00:49:41,979
Damn it.

608
00:49:42,062 --> 00:49:42,938
Get up.

609
00:49:49,027 --> 00:49:49,945
What was that?

610
00:49:50,737 --> 00:49:51,697
Go take a look.

611
00:50:08,797 --> 00:50:10,173
Hey! You…

612
00:50:45,834 --> 00:50:46,668
Hey, Jeong-yo.

613
00:50:47,377 --> 00:50:50,839
Kim only came here
because other guys have seen you around.

614
00:50:50,922 --> 00:50:52,799
He doesn't know which school you go to.

615
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:55,969
So just lay low

616
00:50:56,053 --> 00:50:57,804
and don't show up here again.

617
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:58,805
Got it?

618
00:51:01,808 --> 00:51:02,642
Damn it.

619
00:51:12,235 --> 00:51:14,029
Hey, are you insane?

620
00:51:14,112 --> 00:51:15,739
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

621
00:51:19,242 --> 00:51:20,410
You idiot.

622
00:51:20,494 --> 00:51:22,662
What were you thinking,
getting involved like that?

623
00:51:24,539 --> 00:51:26,500
I couldn't stand by
and let them drag you away.

624
00:51:27,459 --> 00:51:29,377
Stop getting into trouble, will you?

625
00:51:34,007 --> 00:51:35,342
Damn it.

626
00:51:39,846 --> 00:51:41,348
Damn it!

627
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:49,064
Why were those guys after you?

628
00:51:50,065 --> 00:51:51,108
Isn't it obvious?

629
00:51:51,858 --> 00:51:54,361
If the guy who owes you skips town,
you go after his kid.

630
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:57,405
And you have no idea

631
00:51:58,824 --> 00:51:59,908
where your father is?

632
00:52:01,326 --> 00:52:02,994
How much debt are we talking about?

633
00:52:05,038 --> 00:52:05,872
Why?

634
00:52:06,581 --> 00:52:07,833
Are you going to pay it off?

635
00:52:07,916 --> 00:52:09,626
What if they show up again?

636
00:52:10,293 --> 00:52:12,170
You need to come up with a plan.

637
00:52:12,921 --> 00:52:16,466
Coming up with a plan
is useless for someone like me.

638
00:52:18,844 --> 00:52:19,970
Forget it.

639
00:52:21,763 --> 00:52:23,223
So why were you a jerk to me?

640
00:52:24,558 --> 00:52:25,392
Tell me.

641
00:52:26,935 --> 00:52:28,061
Why did you treat me like that?

642
00:52:33,733 --> 00:52:34,568
I'm sorry.

643
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:36,319
It was childish of me.

644
00:52:40,115 --> 00:52:40,991
What?

645
00:52:42,534 --> 00:52:43,910
I mean…

646
00:52:50,584 --> 00:52:51,626
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
TRADITIONAL MARKET

647
00:52:55,213 --> 00:52:56,173
If you're sorry,

648
00:52:57,090 --> 00:52:58,216
come with me somewhere.

649
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:00,510
Where?

650
00:53:01,094 --> 00:53:02,596
Will you come or not?

651
00:53:29,164 --> 00:53:33,460
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

652
00:53:45,764 --> 00:53:46,598
Come in.

653
00:53:56,566 --> 00:53:57,442
What's this?

654
00:53:58,193 --> 00:53:59,444
I never knew this place was here.

655
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:02,864
It used to be a warehouse
where pianos were brought in for repairs.

656
00:54:03,573 --> 00:54:05,200
I've been coming here since I was a kid.

657
00:54:14,668 --> 00:54:17,629
No one would buy that
because it's too old.

658
00:54:17,712 --> 00:54:18,546
CHOI JEONG-YO

659
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:19,839
Which works out great for me.

660
00:54:26,513 --> 00:54:27,597
This is what we're here for.

661
00:54:40,026 --> 00:54:41,486
You played all of these?

662
00:54:42,237 --> 00:54:43,071
Yeah.

663
00:54:44,572 --> 00:54:46,324
After my mom passed away…

664
00:54:48,326 --> 00:54:49,953
I hated playing the piano.

665
00:54:51,121 --> 00:54:52,998
But for some reason,
playing made me happy.

666
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:57,002
That's why I spent a lot of time here.

667
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:07,178
This one doesn't have any notes.

668
00:55:11,683 --> 00:55:12,642
It's a four-hands piece.

669
00:55:14,019 --> 00:55:17,230
I heard it somewhere
and said it was really good,

670
00:55:17,314 --> 00:55:18,898
so my mom got it for me.

671
00:55:22,485 --> 00:55:23,653
But we never got to play it.

672
00:55:25,447 --> 00:55:28,283
Did your mom play the piano well?

673
00:55:30,118 --> 00:55:30,994
Yeah.

674
00:55:33,038 --> 00:55:35,498
She was actually my piano teacher.

675
00:55:41,880 --> 00:55:43,923
Then let's play this before we go.

676
00:55:45,216 --> 00:55:46,092
Right now?

677
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:47,594
Yeah.

678
00:55:50,889 --> 00:55:53,933
This time, you play the secondo,
and I'll play the primo.

679
00:55:54,017 --> 00:55:56,811
You handle the pedal,
and I'll turn the pages.

680
00:55:56,895 --> 00:55:57,854
Okay.

681
00:56:00,607 --> 00:56:01,816
Hold on to this memory.

682
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:03,818
Remember this practice room

683
00:56:04,861 --> 00:56:05,820
and…

684
00:56:07,864 --> 00:56:08,948
today's performance.

685
00:58:02,103 --> 00:58:03,062
Hey, Jeong-yo.

686
00:58:06,191 --> 00:58:07,734
Let's be practice partners.

687
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:11,321
What do you mean?

688
00:58:12,864 --> 00:58:15,158
You said you were too busy
preparing for the competition.

689
00:58:16,659 --> 00:58:18,119
No, I'm not entering.

690
00:58:18,786 --> 00:58:20,622
I want to be your practice partner

691
00:58:20,705 --> 00:58:23,833
and find a way to be happy making music.

692
00:58:24,584 --> 00:58:26,044
You'll help me, right?

693
00:58:43,228 --> 00:58:44,062
No.

694
00:58:48,733 --> 00:58:49,943
Kang Pi-o!

695
00:58:52,529 --> 00:58:54,072
Hey, stop!

696
00:58:54,739 --> 00:58:56,741
Let go of me! Let go!

697
00:58:57,951 --> 00:58:58,826
Enough!

698
00:59:05,375 --> 00:59:06,376
Are you insane?

699
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:08,628
This is all your fault.

700
00:59:10,255 --> 00:59:12,257
It's all your fault!

701
00:59:37,365 --> 00:59:39,492
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

702
00:59:40,076 --> 00:59:41,869
I've decided not to enter the competition.

703
00:59:42,370 --> 00:59:45,582
I don't think I've ever played the piano
because it was fun.

704
00:59:46,583 --> 00:59:47,792
Fine, then quit!

705
00:59:47,875 --> 00:59:49,836
To hell with lessons and school!

706
00:59:50,878 --> 00:59:52,171
His family must be rich.

707
00:59:52,755 --> 00:59:53,923
Give me his number.

708
00:59:54,007 --> 00:59:56,217
Sir, he has nothing to do with this.

709
00:59:56,801 --> 00:59:58,261
So? What do we do now?

710
00:59:58,970 --> 01:00:00,680
Are you uncomfortable around me?

711
01:00:00,763 --> 01:00:02,682
-Where are you?
-You curious?

712
01:00:04,642 --> 01:00:05,476
Kang Pi-o!

713
01:00:08,021 --> 01:00:13,026
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
